import GaloisForLFunctions.RHTower.ThetaCuspHawkingBMEvenSectorSkewPlateauHarmonic

/-!
# The vector-vector and scalar×vector kernels of the horizon plateau, and the sector quartic form

The scalar-sector master field is sourced by the square of the scalar linear mode (`SS`), by the
square of the vector linear mode (`VV`, Laurent master `vvLaurentMaster = A/r + B/r³`), and by
their product. With independent sector amplitudes `aS`, `aV` the two-rate horizon plateau of the
scalar-sector current is the quartic form `aS⁴·P_SS + aS²aV²·P_X + aV⁴·P_VV` in the amplitudes,
with per-harmonic kernels `skewPlateauMu`, `skewPlateauMuCross`, `skewPlateauMuVV` (the last two
defined here by their explicit numerators over the common denominator
`128(2−μ)²(μ−(2s+1)(2s+2))(μ−(2s+4)(2s+5))`, obtained from the same certified current pieces with
the vector-vector Laurent coefficients and sources; the horizon poles cancel for all three).

On the critical line with real harmonic `μ = −l` all three are purely imaginary and their line
forms share the leading structure (`skewPlateauMuVVLine_leading`, `skewPlateauMuCrossLine_leading`):
`P_SS ≈ −(5/64)·t⁹l²(l−4t²)²`, `P_X ≈ −(1/8)·t⁷l²(l−4t²)²(3l+t²)`,
`P_VV ≈ −(1/4)·t⁵l²(l−4t²)²(l−3t²)(l+t²)`, so the leading quartic form is
`−(1/64)·t⁵l²(l−4t²)²·[5t⁴x² + 8t²(3l+t²)xy + 16(l−3t²)(l+t²)y²]` with `x = aS²`, `y = aV²`,
and the bracket factors over the reals, `5t⁴x² + 8t²(3l+t²)xy + 16(l−3t²)(l+t²)y² =
(5t²x − 4(3t²−l)y)(t²x + 4(l+t²)y)` (`skewSectorForm_factor`): its discriminant is the square
`16t⁴(l+2t²)²`. Consequently the vector-vector kernel has **positive** imaginary part on the
bulk harmonics — certified on `40t ≤ l ≤ 2t²`, `t ≥ 50` (`skewPlateauMuVV_line_im_pos`) — where the
scalar-scalar kernel is negative (`skewPlateauMu_line_im_neg`): a pure scalar excitation and a pure
vector excitation give opposite on-line signs of the plateau at every bulk harmonic, so no
amplitude-independent sign law of the clock coefficient can hold; the on-line sign at a harmonic
`l = c·t²` is that of `−(5t²x − 4(3t²−l)y)`, i.e. negative iff `aS² > (4/5)(3−c)·aV²`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

namespace RHTower.D4BMScalarStream

